7. Lunar Demonstration

7.1 Controlled Experiment

LunarChips. Shared preprocessing pipeline with identical reprojection (0.5° grid), band-wise normalization, unified missing-modality handling, and common coordinate system.

Baseline A. Same model, different random seeds → stochastic variance.

Baseline B. Same architecture, different pretraining subsets → data bias.

Baseline C. Different models (Moonstone, Lunar-FM, NASA/IBM LFM), same LunarChips → cross-model discrepancy.

Claim condition.

D_P^{\text{know}} \gg \max\left(D_P^{A}, D_P^{B}\right)

where D_P^{\text{know}} is the observation–knowledge discrepancy in the common observable space O.

7.2 Historical Benchmark Cases

Gap Type Historical Case
Inconsistency Early remote-sensing interpretations of polar volatiles subsequently revised or qualified
Boundary Thermal models fail in permanently shadowed regions
Coverage High-coverage regions with no returned measurements

7.3 Contamination Controls

· Temporal splits for retrieval K (remove post-2010 papers);
· Synthetic gaps by masking a modality or instrument;
· Held-out expert-curated gaps not present in K;
· Closed-book vs. open-book model conditions.

7.4 Step-by-Step Protocol

Phase 1 — Data Assembly. Download Moonstone (28 ch, 128 ppd), Lunar-FM (18 ch, 768-dim), NASA/IBM LFM (30+ layers, 9 instruments). Align to 0.5° grid. Band-wise normalization. Missing-modality masking. Produce LunarChips.

Phase 2 — Frozen Encoder Extraction. Freeze each encoder. Extract embeddings for all tiles. Store with tile identifiers and coordinates.

Phase 3 — Capacity-Constrained Probe Training. Define \mathcal{O} = \{\text{albedo}, T_b, \text{CPR}, \text{neutron count}\}. For each model, train a capacity-constrained non-linear probe f_\theta(z). Fix \theta-complexity budget by nested CV on training block. Validate on calibration block. Report R^2 per observable per model. Proceed only if R^2 > 0.8 for all observables.

Phase 4 — Discrepancy Computation. Compute \hat{o}_1, \hat{o}_2, \hat{o}_3 in \mathcal{O}-space. Compute D_P^{A} (seed variance), D_P^{B} (subset variance), D_P^{\text{model}}, D_P^{\text{obs}}, D_P^{\text{know}}. Report distributions.

Phase 5 — Gate Application. Apply gates D, A, U, P, K. Record pass, confidence, abstention per gate. Compute \mathcal{Q} and \mathcal{G}. Verify N_{\text{eff}} via partial distance correlation.

Phase 6 — Benchmark Evaluation. Compute gap precision, recall, FDR, abstention rate, deferred resolution rate, risk–coverage AUC. Compute Gate Ablation Table with parallel evaluation. Compare to LLM baseline and random baseline. Apply framework-level falsification test.

