9. What the Framework Must NOT Claim

1. Every anomaly is a gap.
2. Every gap is scientifically important.
3. Every hypothesis generated from a gap is novel.
4. Multiple AI models constitute independent evidence.
5. Embeddings have direct physical meaning.
6. Model disagreement proves physical disagreement.
7. Literature absence proves knowledge absence.
8. An LLM can independently certify scientific truth.
9. A candidate gap is a discovery.
10. Unlearning-as-ablation proves constructive generation.
11. Moonstone, Lunar-FM, and NASA/IBM LFM are independent evidence sources. They all use LRO data. The framework's own N_{\text{eff}} computation will demonstrate this. This is not a weakness; it is the strongest argument against naive ensembling in planetary AI.

