Appendix F — Risk–Coverage Analysis

F.1 Definitions

Let $\mathcal{S}$ be the set of all tiles, $\mathcal{Q}$ the deferred set, $\mathcal{G}$ the promoted set, $\mathcal{R}$ the rejected set. Coverage is:

\operatorname{Cov}(\lambda) = \frac{|\{x \in \mathcal{S} \setminus \mathcal{Q}(\lambda) : \text{conf} \geq \lambda\}|}{|\mathcal{S}|},

where $\mathcal{Q}(\lambda)$ is the deferred set at confidence threshold $\lambda$. Risk is:

\operatorname{Risk}(\lambda) = \frac{|\{x \in \mathcal{G}(\lambda) : x \text{ is a false promotion}\}|}{|\mathcal{G}(\lambda)|}.

F.2 Risk–Coverage Curve

The curve $\{(\operatorname{Cov}(\lambda), \operatorname{Risk}(\lambda))\}_{\lambda \in [0,1]}$ is estimated on the calibration block. The area under the risk–coverage curve (AURC) is:

\operatorname{AURC} = \int_0^1 \operatorname{Risk}(\lambda) \, d\operatorname{Cov}(\lambda).

Proposition F.1. Under the conditional proposition (Appendix C.1), $\operatorname{Risk}(0) \leq \alpha$ and $\operatorname{Risk}(1) \leq \alpha$.

Proof. At $\lambda = 0$, all tiles are covered except those deferred. The risk among non-deferred is bounded by the conditional proposition. At $\lambda = 1$, only tiles with confidence $1$ are covered, which is a subset of the non-deferred set. $\square$

F.3 Deferred-Set Resolution

For each abstention type $\alpha_s$, the resolution rate is:

\operatorname{Res}(\alpha_s) = \frac{|\{x \in \mathcal{Q}_{\alpha_s} : \text{status}(x) \in \{\text{promoted}, \text{rejected}\}\}|}{|\mathcal{Q}_{\alpha_s}|}.

The deferred-set stratification is reported alongside the risk–coverage curve.

