Appendix H — Reference Measure Construction: Full Protocol

H.1 Retrieval

For each observable $o \in \mathcal{O}$ and tile $x$:

1. Query the literature corpus with $\Sigma(x)$, $\Lambda(x)$, and $o$.
2. Retrieve the top-$K_{\text{ret}}$ documents by BM25 + dense retrieval fusion (RRF).
3. Filter by scope-Jaccard $Q > 0.5$ and normalized replication $R > 0.3$.
4. Deduplicate by DOI and by semantic similarity $> 0.9$.

H.2 Range Extraction

For each retained source $s$, extract the reported range $[o_{\min}^{(s)}, o_{\max}^{(s)}]$ and its provenance. Where the source reports a distribution, extract the mean and standard deviation. Aggregate across sources via a weighted mixture:

P_0^{\text{lit}}(o) = \sum_s \omega_s \, \mathcal{N}(o; \mu_s, \sigma_s^2), \quad \omega_s \propto R_s \cdot Q_s.

H.3 Forward-Model Augmentation

Where a forward model $\mathcal{F}$ exists, convolve its predictive distribution with the literature mixture:

P_0(o \mid x) = \int P_0^{\text{lit}}(o - u) \, P_{\mathcal{F}}(u \mid \theta(x)) \, du.

The convolution is computed numerically via Monte Carlo with $10^4$ samples.

H.4 Background Calibration

For observables without a forward model, estimate a background distribution from well-understood regions with matched $(\Sigma, \Lambda)$:

P_0^{\text{bg}}(o) = \frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}|} \sum_{x' \in \mathcal{B}} K_h(o - o(x')),

where $\mathcal{B}$ is the matched background set and $K_h$ is a Gaussian kernel with bandwidth selected by Silverman's rule.

H.5 Validation

The reference measure is validated against held-out known observations $\{(x_i, o_i)\}_{i=1}^{n_{\text{val}}}$:

\text{Coverage} = \frac{1}{n_{\text{val}}} \sum_{i=1}^{n_{\text{val}}} \mathbb{1}\left[o_i \in \left[P_0^{-1}(0.025), P_0^{-1}(0.975)\right]\right].

The reference measure is validated if $\text{Coverage} \in [0.90, 0.98]$. If outside this range, $P_0$ is recalibrated or the tile is deferred.

H.6 Failure Modes

Failure mode Detection Action
Empty retrieval pool $ \mathcal{P}_{\text{ret}}(x)
Conflicting sources $\max_s \mu_s - \min_s \mu_s > 2 \sum_s \sigma_s$ Defer with $\alpha_{\text{conflict}}$
Reference shift KL$(P_0 \| P_0^{\text{historical}}) > 1.0$ Defer with $\alpha_{\text{ood}}$
Validation failure Coverage outside $[0.90, 0.98]$ Recalibrate or defer

