Appendix I — Probe Capacity Selection

I.1 Global Capacity Budget

The capacity budget $C$ is selected once, on the reference model $i^* = \arg\min_i \operatorname{median}_o R^2_{\text{probe}}(i, o)$ evaluated at a pilot $C_0$. The selection minimizes:

C^* = \arg\min_C \left[ \frac{1}{|\mathcal{O}|} \sum_{o \in \mathcal{O}} \left( R^2_{\text{probe}}(i^*, o; C) - R^2_{\text{target}} \right)^2 \right],

with $R^2_{\text{target}} = 0.85$. The nested CV protocol is:

· Outer: 5-fold geographic split.
· Inner: 3-fold temporal split within each outer fold.
· Regularization $\lambda$: selected by the 1-SE rule.

I.2 Probe Classes

Class Form Regularization
KRR-Laplacian $f(z) = \sum_k \alpha_k \exp(-\|z - z_k\|_1 / \sigma)$ $\lambda \|\alpha\|^2$
KRR-Gaussian $f(z) = \sum_k \alpha_k \exp(-\|z - z_k\|_2^2 / (2\sigma^2))$ $\lambda \|\alpha\|^2$
MLP-Spectral 2-layer, spectral norm $\|W_1\|_2 \leq s_1, \|W_2\|_2 \leq s_2$ $s_1 s_2 \leq C$

I.3 Comparability Test

For each model $i$ and observable $o$:

R^2_{\text{probe}}(i, o; C^*) = 1 - \frac{\sum_x (o(x) - \hat{o}_i(x))^2}{\sum_x (o(x) - \bar{o})^2}.

Model $i$ is retained if:

\min_{o \in \mathcal{O}} R^2_{\text{probe}}(i, o; C^*) > 0.8.

If a model fails this condition, it is excluded from the ensemble and $N_{\text{eff}}$ is recomputed on the retained set.

I.4 Sensitivity Analysis

The sensitivity of $R^2$ to $C$ is reported as:

\mathcal{S}(C) = \frac{\partial R^2_{\text{probe}}}{\partial \log C}.

If $|\mathcal{S}(C^*)| > 0.1$, the capacity budget is considered sensitive and the probe class is re-examined. A model whose $R^2$ is highly sensitive to $C$ is flagged as possibly under- or over-parameterized relative to the observable.

