Appendix J — Observability Model Calibration

J.1 Components

O_{\text{geom}}(x) = \frac{\cos \theta_i(x)}{\max_{x'} \cos \theta_i(x')}, \quad O_{\text{SNR}}(x) = \frac{\text{SNR}(x)}{\max_{x'} \text{SNR}(x')}, \quad O_{\text{coverage}}(x) = \frac{\text{cov}(x)}{\max_{x'} \text{cov}(x')}.

J.2 Multiplicative vs. Joint

The multiplicative form is a working hypothesis. If the validation reveals systematic deviation, the model is replaced by:

O(x) = g\!\left(O_{\text{geom}}(x), O_{\text{SNR}}(x), O_{\text{coverage}}(x)\right),

with $g$ fit by isotonic regression on held-out known observations. The choice is made by comparing the two models on the validation Brier score:

\operatorname{BS}(O) = \frac{1}{n_{\text{val}}} \sum_{i=1}^{n_{\text{val}}} \left(O(x_i) - \mathbb{1}[x_i \text{ observed}]\right)^2.

The multiplicative model is retained if $\operatorname{BS}(O_{\text{mult}}) \leq \operatorname{BS}(O_{\text{joint}}) + 0.01$.

J.3 False Positive and False Negative Rates

Let $\tau_O = 0.9$. The observability model's FPR and FNR are:

\operatorname{FPR}_O = \frac{|\{x : O(x) > \tau_O, \text{Observed}(x) = 1\}|}{|\{x : \text{Observed}(x) = 1\}|},

\operatorname{FNR}_O = \frac{|\{x : O(x) \leq \tau_O, \text{Observed}(x) = 0\}|}{|\{x : \text{Observed}(x) = 0\}|}.

Both are estimated on the held-out validation set. If $\operatorname{FPR}_O > 0.10$ or $\operatorname{FNR}_O > 0.10$, the observability model is recalibrated before use.

