Appendix L — Framework-Level Falsification: Extended Protocol

L.1 Frozen Benchmark

The benchmark is frozen at $N = 10{,}000$ tiles with:

· Temporal holdout: 3,000 tiles whose confirming observations appeared after 2015 (excluded from $K$).
· Spatial holdout: 2,000 tiles in regions observed by ShadowCam after the foundation models' training cutoff.
· Instrument holdout: 1,000 tiles observed by instruments not in the training corpus.
· In-domain: 4,000 tiles from well-understood regions, serving as a calibration set.

L.2 Test Statistic

\operatorname{P@}k = \frac{|\{\text{top-}k \text{ promoted gaps}\} \cap \{\text{retrodicted confirmed observations}\}|}{k},

for $k \in \{10, 50, 100\}$.

L.3 Baselines

Random-anomaly baseline. Promote $k$ tiles uniformly at random from the candidate set.

Retrieval-augmented LLM baseline. Prompt a strong LLM with the top-$k$ retrieved documents for each tile and the tile's $D_P^{\text{know}}$. Rank tiles by the LLM's stated confidence that the tile is anomalous. Promote the top $k$.

L.4 Paired Bootstrap

For each $k$, compute the paired difference:

\Delta_k = \operatorname{P@}k_{\text{ECSD}} - \max\left(\operatorname{P@}k_{\text{random}}, \operatorname{P@}k_{\text{LLM}}\right).

The bootstrap distribution of $\Delta_k$ is estimated by resampling tiles with replacement $B = 10{,}000$ times. The test rejects the null $H_0: \Delta_k \leq 0$ at level $\alpha = 0.05$ if the $5$th percentile of the bootstrap distribution exceeds $0$.

L.5 Multiplicity Correction

For $k \in \{10, 50, 100\}$, apply Holm–Bonferroni:

\alpha_k^{\text{Holm}} = \frac{\alpha}{3 - \operatorname{rank}(k) + 1}.

The framework-level falsification criterion is:

\text{ECSD fails} \iff \nexists k : \Delta_k > 0 \text{ at } \alpha_k^{\text{Holm}}.

L.6 Sensitivity Analysis

Report $\Delta_k$ as a function of:

· The block size $|B|$;
· The power calibrator $\kappa$;
· The KC threshold $\tau_{\text{KC}}$;
· The uncertainty threshold $\tau_U$.

The sensitivity analysis identifies which hyperparameter most affects the framework-level outcome.

